  "habitat": "Usually solitary at forest fringes, in riverine forest and valley bush.",
  "summary": "A fairly common resident. Streaky head, scaly throat and breast usually washed yellow, grey back, yellow bars on the wings and paler underparts. The call is a high foyt-foyt-foyt, or a purring trrrrrrrr from a call-site, rising at the end. It sometimes guides to bees’ nests and otherwise hawks insects. The Kemp code RB was left unchanged.",
